Z||000000||Gold-86SE||07-19-2001||03:27 PM||||<BR>A few days back I posted this question <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011985.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011985.html</A> <P>Last night I brainstormed that maybe my fuel pump is not functioning at the proper pressure and the books say 40.5 to 47 pounds of pressure should be seen.<P>At idle I am running 36 or 38, and upon increased rpm speed, i still run at the 36-38 range.  I am still feeling a bump while driving, will a low fuel pressure cause this problem?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-19-2001||04:44 PM||||I would say no however I wonder if maybe just perhaps you have a dirty fuel filter?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Toddster||07-19-2001||09:05 PM||||The average range of operation for a 2.8 V-6 is usually around 37 PSI. So I would be surprised if it is causing problems at this pressure. 45 is recommended for a 3.1 engine. If the car is hesitating try a new fuel filter. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||07-20-2001||09:11 AM||||<BR>Well, I guess I will try a new filter and while in the process, put new plugs and wires  or just wires on the engine.  Thanks for the ideas.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ironhedno3||07-20-2001||09:49 AM||||if its overfueling dont forget to change your oil and filter also||||reg||6
